<title>USA: McDonnell gains orders for two MD-90s.</title>
<headline>McDonnell gains orders for two MD-90s.</headline>
<dateline>LONG BEACH, Calif. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp on Monday said AMC Aviation, an Egyptian charter flight operator, ordered two MD-90-30 extended range airplanes.</p>
<p>The aircraft, worth about $100 million, are scheduled for delivery in August and in October 1998.</p>
<p>AMC Aviation, formed in 1994, currently operates a fleet of three aircraft, providing charter service between Egypt and destinations in France, Germany and Belgium.</p>
</text>
